### CRIT-003 — Cookies Lack `Secure` Flag (Transmitted Over HTTP)

**Severity:** 🔴 Critical  
**Category:** Security  
**Location:** [auth.py:170-171](file:///g:/Languages/Projects/Healthcare%20AI/R1/backend/app/routers/auth.py#L170-L171) (and all `set_cookie` calls)

**Problem:** All `response.set_cookie(...)` calls set `httponly=True` and `samesite="lax"` but **never set `secure=True`**. This means cookies containing JWT tokens will be transmitted over plain HTTP connections, making them interceptable via MITM attacks.

**Recommended fix:** Add `secure=True` to all `set_cookie` calls (at minimum in production). Make this configurable based on `DEBUG` setting.

**Production impact:** Session hijacking via network sniffing

