### CRIT-004 — Hardcoded Credentials in Login Form (Frontend)

**Severity:** 🔴 Critical  
**Category:** Security / UX  
**Location:** [LoginModal.jsx:22-23](file:///g:/Languages/Projects/Healthcare%20AI/R1/frontend-react/src/components/LoginModal.jsx#L22-L23)

**Problem:**
```javascript
const [email, setEmail] = useState('gaurav@lifeos.com');
const [password, setPassword] = useState('password123');
```
The login form is pre-filled with a real user's email and **plaintext password**. This ships to all users of the frontend.

**Recommended fix:** Set default values to empty strings: `useState('')`

**Production impact:** Any visitor can see and use these credentials

