### CRIT-008 — Admin Routes Not Protected by Role Check in Frontend

**Severity:** 🔴 Critical  
**Category:** Security / Authorization  
**Location:** [App.jsx:98-118](file:///g:/Languages/Projects/Healthcare%20AI/R1/frontend-react/src/App.jsx#L98-L118)

**Problem:** Admin routes (`/admin/*`) have no frontend route guard verifying the user's role. Any authenticated user can navigate to `/admin` and access the admin panel UI. While backend admin endpoints use `require_role("admin")`, the frontend exposes the full admin interface to non-admin users, leaking admin UI structure and potentially allowing actions if any backend endpoint is missing the role check.

**Recommended fix:** Add a `ProtectedAdminRoute` wrapper that checks user role before rendering admin components.

