### HIGH-002 — Google OAuth Auto-Registers Without Email Verification

**Severity:** 🟠 High  
**Category:** Security  
**Location:** [auth.py:215-229](file:///g:/Languages/Projects/Healthcare%20AI/R1/backend/app/routers/auth.py#L215-L229)

**Problem:** Google OAuth creates users with `is_verified` defaulting to model default (False per model, but the code never sets it to True). The flow then skips the verification check since it doesn't explicitly set the flag, potentially creating unverified Google users.

---

### HIGH-003 — Token Version Not Checked on Google/Face Login Token Generation

**Severity:** 🟠 High  
**Category:** Security  
**Location:** [auth.py:242-243](file:///g:/Languages/Projects/Healthcare%20AI/R1/backend/app/routers/auth.py#L242-L243), [auth.py:596-597](file:///g:/Languages/Projects/Healthcare%20AI/R1/backend/app/routers/auth.py#L596-L597)

**Problem:** `create_access_token(user.id, user.role)` is called without `token_version=user.token_version`. This means tokens generated via Google/Face login won't include the correct version, and the `get_current_user_id` dependency will reject them if `token_version` defaults to 1 but the user's version is different.

