## 8. Database Audit

### Schema Problems
- **Redundant columns:** `User.is_verified` AND `User.email_verified` serve the same purpose
- **Redundant columns:** `User.is_phone_verified` AND `User.phone_verified`
- **Misleading defaults:** `UserProfile.age=30`, `gender="Male"`, `blood_type="O+"` — healthcare app should require these
- **No indexes** on `health_entries.user_id` + `category` (common query pattern)
- **No indexes** on `medical_records.user_id` + `created_at` (listing query)
- **No unique constraint** on `health_entries` to prevent duplicate entries for same metric/time
- **Cascading:** `User.profile` has `cascade="all, delete-orphan"` — good. But `LoginHistory`, `ChatMessage`, etc. only have FK `ondelete="CASCADE"` — should be verified

### Query Problems
- **N+1 risk:** Dashboard loads medicines, appointments, records, and family members in separate queries
- **In-memory filtering:** Medical records search filters in Python after loading all records
- **No pagination:** `GET /trackers/health-data`, `GET /records`, `GET /medicines` load ALL records
- **Missing water query:** Dashboard never queries the water intake table

### Migration Problems
- No Alembic migration scripts found — relying entirely on `create_all()` and raw `ALTER TABLE`
- Pseudo-migrations in both `main.py` lifespan and `database.py` `init_db()` — duplicated and unversioned

